-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Owen Lin &lt;owenlin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="448839" owner_email="mka@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/39/448839/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8228c6406bcbc3c9ac2f5f122d35bf84edce9f85" commit="b137c588c61b721da0e884c4359cf6e03c5d4ca1" commit_message="remove profile=llvm and USE=clang for llvm builders.  THe llvm migration is complete, we can remove the llvm profile from these builders. We also set to use clang to build chrome by default, so there is no need to set USE=clang.  BUG=chromium:699594 TEST=run_test passes.  Change-Id: I8228c6406bcbc3c9ac2f5f122d35bf84edce9f85 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/451551 Commit-Ready: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Manoj Gupta &lt;manojgupta@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="451551" owner_email="yunlian@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/51/451551/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I16ad520573302a8f9a713dab2ba8400690ff03c7" commit="4f8d202b1d65162a99ad2d455c54e2dbd85bcfa3" commit_message="Add a functional test for firmware update  The existing unit test is useful for finding simple problems. But there is value in having an larger test which actually runs the firmware update to make sure it behaves as expected.  To make this work we need a firmware image. We also need to mock out some of the tools:  - crossystem - used to display info about the system we are running on - flashrom - used to access the SPI firmware - vpd - used to access the VPD area of firmware  BUG=chromium:690573 TEST=FEATURES=test emerge-reef --nodeps  chromeos-firmware-reef Outside chroot: PYTHONPATH=~/cosarm python pack_firmware_functest.py  Change-Id: I16ad520573302a8f9a713dab2ba8400690ff03c7 Signed-off-by: Simon Glass &lt;sjg@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/450855 Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="450855" owner_email="sjg@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/firmware" ref="refs/changes/55/450855/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I33b372bbdfacf8bf6378876f560187af75a344dc" commit="eaff413ce9f2aa170769c17e6d373e9711751823" commit_message="README: convert to markdown for gitiles  BUG=None TEST=looked at the output in gitiles  Change-Id: I33b372bbdfacf8bf6378876f560187af75a344dc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/428851 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Chan &lt;benchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="428851" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/daisydog" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/daisydog" ref="refs/changes/51/428851/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib307547a4c4d6300ccf018b33aee4db7a4f364f8" commit="23cb3ac78524ac66e1fb13da111824bb956c2892" commit_message="common: Ensure print_build_string() prints short strings properly.  Pass &quot;full_build_string&quot; to ccprintf() as expected. I believe that this code only worked previosly due to blind luck; the compiler allocated &quot;full_build_string&quot; on the stack in such a way that it was available at the end of the call frame for ccprintf().  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=make -j buildall  Change-Id: Ib307547a4c4d6300ccf018b33aee4db7a4f364f8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/451084 Commit-Ready: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Carl Hamilton &lt;carlh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="451084" owner_email="carlh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/84/451084/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I33d4a811f9bd9b2c4df27071534a0d5bce1335cc" commit="2719ce1bb4252479e323ede106685266f807a45e" commit_message="power_SuspendStress: stay awake up to 8 seconds in between S2Rs  The current test runs for 4 hours, staying awake between 0 and 3 seconds between S2R attempts. This doesn't seem long enough to guarantee we'll keep an SSH connection alive. Particularly, when using the default autotest parameters (ServerAliveInterval=900, ServerAliveCountMax=3), then we often can see a 4 hour test have its SSH session terminated at about 45 minutes.  One way to combat this is to increase the window of values in which we select a random &quot;resume time&quot;; if we wait up to 8 seconds, then we will occasionally give the DUT enough time to service the network properly.  BUG=b:35648179 TEST=test_that power_SuspendStress.4hours  Change-Id: I33d4a811f9bd9b2c4df27071534a0d5bce1335cc Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/450785 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="450785" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/85/450785/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I0944a78f6309994027de726a296c858524ae3ccf" commit="f6fe2517a4b0402eec1d120f55362495d3effa67" commit_message="CHROMIUM: coreboot: Update coreboot table ACPI ID  The coreboot project now has an official ACPI ID and will report the memory address of the coreboot tables.  Add the new BOOT0000 ID to the list, while retaining support for the older ID that was used on some Chromium devices.  BUG=b:36053664 TEST=boot on Eve with TOT coreboot and check for /sys/firmware/log  Change-Id: I0944a78f6309994027de726a296c858524ae3ccf Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/450836 Commit-Ready: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="450836" owner_email="dlaurie@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/36/450836/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I51fb9aa17d5d9eaf15d54df9f45db12b503b31b9" commit="73dc3089a6b133ebee93bcc7c5a2657c12c3de4d" commit_message="snappy: Lock EC and PD communication  Follow reef setting  BUG=none BRANCH=reef TEST=make buildall  Change-Id: I51fb9aa17d5d9eaf15d54df9f45db12b503b31b9 Signed-off-by: Bruce.Wan &lt;Bruce.Wan@quantatw.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/444591 Commit-Ready: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="444591" owner_email="Bruce.Wan@quantatw.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.goog